      "message": "[Major] The password still reaches the log here, at ERROR level.\n\n`validation_exc.errors()` is logged without sanitizing. For a missing field, pydantic v2 puts the whole dict of that level into `input`. Reproduced with `RouteWithLogging` and a body that lacks one required field:\n\n```\nERROR ... Validation exception [..., {\u0027type\u0027: \u0027missing\u0027, \u0027loc\u0027: (\u0027body\u0027, \u0027otp\u0027), \u0027msg\u0027: \u0027Field required\u0027,\n  \u0027input\u0027: {\u0027email\u0027: \u0027john.smith@x\u0027, \u0027password\u0027: \u0027S3cr3t!\u0027}}]\n```\n\nThis line predates the change, but it is squarely within WT-2211\u0027s scope (\"mask secrets in adapter logs\"), and this one is ERROR level, so it shows up in production, not only with DEBUG on. The same unsanitized `str(validation_exc.errors())` is also echoed to the client in the 422 body above.\n\nSuggested fix: `logging.error(f\"Validation exception {sanitize_data(validation_exc.errors())}\")`. `sanitize_data` already recurses into lists and dicts, and turns the `loc` tuples into lists. Please also add a test, e.g. `POST /session` with a required field missing, asserting the password is not in the log.",
